<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1996 grain shipments detailed.</title>
<headline>Russian 1996 grain shipments detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's imports of wheat and wheat-rye blends over 1996 totalled 2.7 million tonnes and were valued at $573.6 million, according to State Customs Committee figures on Monday.</p>
<p>The data, carried by Interfax news agency, put Russia's wheat-flour imports last year at 687,400 tonnes, worth $215.5 million.</p>
<p>Russia's 1996 barley imports, nearly all from Kazakhstan, were 1.4 million tonnes and valued at $78.5 million.</p>
<p>Rye imports last year were 264,500 tonnes and cost $43.3 million, with all the deliveries from Ukraine.</p>
<p>Russian exports of wheat and wheat-rye blends last year were 343,000 tonnes and were valued at $62.1 million.</p>
<p>Wheat-flour exports, valued at $36.3 million, were 103,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>State Customs Committee figures do not include unregistered transactions.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
